    {
      "abstract": "(Color online) $\\Upsilon$(1S+2S+3S) (a) and $\\Upsilon$(1S) (b) $R_{AA}$ vs. $N_{part}$ in $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 193 GeV U+U collisions (solid circles), compared to 200 GeV RHIC Au+Au (solid squares [13] and hollow crosses [32]), and 2.76 TeV LHC Pb+Pb data (solid diamonds [33]). A 95% lower confidence bound is indicated for the 30-60% centrality U+U data (see text). Each point is plotted at the center of its bin. Centrality integrated (0-60%) U+U and Au+Au data are also shown as open circles and squares, respectively. ",
